# Arithmetic Holography of the Modular Horizon

Umbrella for the holographic layer over the modular horizon: seeds of the modular map, their completed
transforms, position rigidity and the every-seed receiver; cavity families, the pair form, the Baire
reduction of one-mode noncancellation (B109) to pairs of cavity modes and its converse; the pair entries
as Rankin–Selberg series of two cusp forms; momentum universality of the resonances (Rademacher image
sums and Whittaker coefficients); the dual side has no sign (one-sided bounds are two-sided); the odd
cavity sees every resonance (B109 for cavity functions) and is a complete cuspidal receiver; pairs of
Maass cusp eigenforms see every resonance, so one cavity function of Maass forms is a complete receiver;
the resonance Krein form of the cavity has infinite index of both signs at every resonance, while the
reflection Krein form has exactly one negative square at each off-line zero (RH ⟺ positivity); the
ringdown rate of every seed with exponentially decaying completed transform is its zero-free region, and
RH ⟺ every two-mode cavity energy rings down at `y^{3/4−ε}` (Zagier's theorem for the cavity); one
cuspidal function of Maass forms is a sharp receiver: RH ⟺ its energy rings down at `y^{3/4−ε}`. See
`ArithmeticHolographyOfTheModularHorizon/README.md`.
